>>
>
If so why not consider objects as assertions or even properties? This will
quickly destroy the whole system of variable types leaving only  their
interactions relevant.

We don't usually think of living things as "happening", especially since we
>> have the more specific "jmive" for them, But in any case, I'm now not ha=
ppy
>> with "same type as" for comparatives. I realized that anything can be
